    "body": "Closes #64.\n\nThe backup-metadata workflow was pushing to the backups/metadata branch using the built-in GITHUB_TOKEN. GitHub suppresses workflow triggers from events caused by GITHUB_TOKEN to prevent infinite loops, so the mirror workflow was not being triggered automatically after each backup.\n\n## Change\n- Use the METADATA_BACKUP_TOKEN secret (a Personal Access Token) in the push step\n- Rewrite the origin remote URL to include the token before pushing\n\n## Why this works\nA PAT is treated by GitHub as a regular user action, so it triggers other workflows normally.\n\n## Also\nAdded detailed Arabic comments explaining every step and the reasoning behind using a PAT instead of the built-in token.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-26T01:20:09Z",
